386→                        <div id="content">If $n$ distinct points in $\mathbb{R}^2$ form a convex polygon then some vertex has at least $\lfloor \frac{n}{2}\rfloor$ different distances to other vertices.</div>
387→                        <div id="problem_id"><a href="/982">#982</a>: <a href="#cite-Er46b-982" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('Er46b','982'); return false;">[Er46b]</a><a href="#cite-Er75f-982" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('Er75f','982'); return false;">[Er75f,p.100]</a><a href="#cite-Er87b-982" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('Er87b','982'); return false;">[Er87b,p.175]</a><a href="#cite-ErFi94-982" onclick="event.preventDefault();addNewBox('ErFi94','982'); return false;">[ErFi94]</a></div>
